Title: Type of a generic is not narrowed
Description: ### 🔎 Search Terms

generic narrowed class instance enum

### 🕗 Version & Regression Information

- This is the behavior in every version I tried, and I reviewed the FAQ for entries about narrowed.


### ⏯ Playground Link

_No response_

### 💻 Code

```ts
enum Tag {
  A,
  B,
  C,
}

interface InterfaceByTag {
  [Tag.A]: {
    type: string;
  };
  [Tag.B]: {
    type: number;
  };
  [Tag.C]: {
    type: boolean;
  };
}

class C<
  T extends Tag = Tag,
> {
  tag: T;
  type: InterfaceByTag[T]["type"];

  constructor(tag: T, type: InterfaceByTag[T]["type"]) {
    this.tag = tag;
    this.type = type;
  }
}

const tagIsA = new C(Tag.A, "string");
const tagIsAError = new C(Tag.A, 123);

function test(instance: C) {
  switch (instance.tag) {
    case Tag.A: {
      const type = instance.type; // should get string, but get string | number | boolean.
      break;
    }
    case Tag.B: {
      const type = instance.type; // Same as above
      break;
    }
    case Tag.C: {
      const type = instance.type; // Same as above
      break;
    }
  }
}
```


### 🙁 Actual behavior

It is not narrowed in the switch statement. In all case, the type of `instance.type` is `string | number | boolean`.

### 🙂 Expected behavior

I think the specific type has been identified In the switch statement. What I expected:
```ts
  switch (instance.tag) {
    case Tag.A: {
      const type = instance.type; // string
      break;
    }
    case Tag.B: {
      const type = instance.type; // number
      break;
    }
    case Tag.C: {
      const type = instance.type; // boolean
      break;
    }
  }
```

